 "verdict_schedule": "THE_SCHEDULE_MOVES_RETURN_MORE_THAN_RISK",
 "verdict_why": "Keeping the hedge the right size is almost free: the busiest schedule trades 29.5% of book notional a year and the quietest 20.1%, a difference of 0.094 notional a year, which at 1.0 bp per side costs 0.0029 pp of return a year -- 17 times below the 0.05 pp noise line. You would have to pay 53 bp per side before that difference reached the line. The schedule barely moves risk either: annualised volatility spans 0.34 pp across all eight (11.15%..11.50%) against a 1.05 pp span in annual return. The return spread is not the cadence -- it is whether the size chases the beta at all: the two schedules that hold one size finish at 12.21% and 12.06%, above every one of the 6 schedules that follow the beta (best 11.79%). The chasing itself costs 0.97 pp a year in this window (the arithmetic: the size you trail is slightly high in the periods the hedge then earns, and 0.97 pp a year is what that covariance subtracts)."
}
